Using GitHub Actions? Make your life easier with built-in actions!

When setting up CI/CD in GitHub, you don’t need to start from scratch. GitHub provides ready-to-use actions for common tasks — no extra setup needed.

Here are a few popular ones:

🔹 actions/checkout – Pulls your code into the workflow
🔹 actions/setup-node – Sets up Node.js so you can run JavaScript tools
🔹 actions/setup-python – Prepares a Python environment
🔹 actions/cache – Speeds things up by saving dependencies
🔹 actions/upload-artifact – Share files across workflow steps

💬 These are simple, reliable, and maintained by GitHub itself.

Here’s an example of using two built-in actions:

steps:
  - uses: actions/checkout@v4
  - uses: actions/setup-node@v4
    with:
      node-version: '18'

They’re super handy and help you focus on what really matters: building and shipping faster.
